; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Moire Magic
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     moire, interference, circles, lines, optical illusion
; SUMMARY:  Slides two sets of thin rings across each other so that ghostly bands appear and change where they cross.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Two sets of thin circles, all the same distance apart, are drawn
;   with their centers a little way apart. Where the rings cross,
;   your eye sees dark and light bands that nobody drew. That is a
;   moire pattern. The centers slowly move apart, and the ghost
;   bands multiply as they do.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Change MAXSHIFT to move the two centers
;   further apart, or GAP to space the rings out.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARC 360 r draws a full circle round the turtle without moving it
;   * evenly spaced shapes, using a FOR loop with a step
;   * how two simple regular patterns combine into a complex one
;   * animation by wiping the screen with CLEAN and drawing again
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Stop at a shift of 0. The magic disappears. Why?
;   * Make one set of rings red and the other blue.
;   * Write a FAN procedure: straight lines from one corner, a degree
;     apart. Draw two fans from nearby corners and see what happens.
; ============================================================

make "gap 8
make "maxshift 90

; Rings from radius GAP up to MAXR, all centered on (x, y).
; ARC draws round the turtle, so we only have to stand in the middle.
to rings :x :y :maxr
  penup setxy :x :y pendown
  for [r :gap :maxr :gap] [arc 360 :r]
end

; Two sets of rings, :shift steps left and right of the center.
to picture :shift
  clean
  rings minus :shift 0 480
  rings :shift 0 480
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 250 245]
setpencolor [30 30 70]
setpensize 2
for [s 0 :maxshift 1] [
  picture :s
  wait 3
]
